# MiceCam Project Index

## Overview
- `cmd/micecam_ui/`: Native Qt/QML desktop application entry, QML scene, and UI-facing controller.
- `cmd/gui/`: Legacy Python/PyQt and web-based UI implementations kept for reference and fallback.
- `internal/`: Core C++ capture, pipeline, storage, and decoder logic.
- `bindings/`: Python bindings for the native C++ core.
- `tests/`: C++ and Python automated tests.
- `docs/requirements/`: Product requirements and acceptance criteria.
- `docs/adr/`: Architecture decision records.
- `docs/plan/`: Phase-level implementation plans.
- `docs/reports/`: Review and implementation reports.
- `docs/wikis/`: Architecture and design knowledge base.

## Current UI Stack
- Current shipping native UI entry: `cmd/micecam_ui/main.cpp`
- Current QML scene: `cmd/micecam_ui/qml/main.qml`
- Shared QML components: `cmd/micecam_ui/qml/components/`
- QML theme tokens: `cmd/micecam_ui/qml/theme/`
- UI state bridge: `cmd/micecam_ui/PipelineController.h`
- Camera inventory model: `cmd/micecam_ui/CameraInventoryModel.h`
- Recording setup and preflight helpers: `cmd/micecam_ui/RecordingSetup.h`
- Live preview provider: `cmd/micecam_ui/VideoFrameProvider.h`
- Native app preflight tests: `tests/ui/native_app_preflight_test.cpp`
- Legacy desktop UI reference: `cmd/gui/gui/main_window.py`
- Native production integration requirements: `docs/requirements/native-app-production-integration.md`
- Native worker runtime ADR: `docs/adr/0001-native-worker-process-runtime.md`
- Native production phase plan: `docs/plan/phase-native-app-integration.md`
- Native runtime architecture notes: `docs/wikis/native-app-runtime-architecture.md`

## Notable Constraints
- Active QML UI has been refactored into a preview-first workspace with reusable components and a tokenized theme layer.
- Camera inventory, capability-driven selection, and controller-side preflight now exist in the native UI path, but worker-process supervision remains follow-up integration work.
- Legacy Python UI remains the strongest reference for worker isolation and preview budget strategy.
- Existing git worktree contains unrelated local changes under `3rdParty/depthai-core`.
